\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Box-size convergence test for the Rigid Cylinder Campaign at $f = 2.6$, $\beta = 1.0$ (3 seeds each). Mean $\lambda /W_{\rm  core}$ decreases from $4.22 \pm 0.34$ at $L_x = 8\,W$ to $2.70 \pm 0.59$ at $L_x = 16\,W$. At $L_x = 32\,W$ (red triangle), all three seeds undergo single-peak global collapse at $t \approx 0.056\,t_{\rm  J}$, yielding no measurable $\lambda /W_{\rm  core}$ (``N/A''). The transition from multi-peak beading to single global collapse between $L_x = 16$ and $32$ is driven by the larger initial power in the $n=1$ turbulent mode at $L_x = 32$; the $L_x = 16$ values should be treated as upper limits. Error bars = standard deviation across 3 seeds; green band marks the HGBS window $[2.52, 3.08]$.}}{17}{figure.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:RC_convergence}{{21}{17}{Box-size convergence test for the Rigid Cylinder Campaign at $f = 2.6$, $\beta = 1.0$ (3 seeds each). Mean $\lambda /W_{\rm core}$ decreases from $4.22 \pm 0.34$ at $L_x = 8\,W$ to $2.70 \pm 0.59$ at $L_x = 16\,W$. At $L_x = 32\,W$ (red triangle), all three seeds undergo single-peak global collapse at $t \approx 0.056\,t_{\rm J}$, yielding no measurable $\lambda /W_{\rm core}$ (``N/A''). The transition from multi-peak beading to single global collapse between $L_x = 16$ and $32$ is driven by the larger initial power in the $n=1$ turbulent mode at $L_x = 32$; the $L_x = 16$ values should be treated as upper limits. Error bars = standard deviation across 3 seeds; green band marks the HGBS window $[2.52, 3.08]$}{figure.21}{}}
